   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Accordion Unfold\n\nA tight paper zigzag unfolds sideways into a flat card with the logo printed across it. The placeholder lockup is a stand-in: a host prints its own logo by replacing the .au-print contents in the script.\n\nCategory: logo-stings. Length: 2.2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A print, stationery, travel or editorial brand wants a tactile reveal, like opening a folded brochure or map.\n- Your logo should sit on a card or label rather than float on the background.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The logo should float freely on the background instead of on a card: use spotlight or anamorphic-flare.\n- The paper motion is a scene change, not a logo reveal: use page-turn.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Wordmark, default \"studio\"\n- panels (number, 2-12): Panels, default 6\n- color (color): Paper, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- shade (number, 0-1): Shade, default 0.55\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- fold_angle (number, 0-89): Fold angle, default 82\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
